      "title": "Qt: activateWindow when asking about unsaved packets",
      "message": "Qt: activateWindow when asking about unsaved packets\n\nWireshark might not be the active application when testing if the\ncapture file can be closed. E.g., on Windows, multiple Wireshark\nprocesses can be open, another application have focus, and the user\nright-click on the Wireshark icon and select \"Close all windows.\"\n\nWhen there's only a single Wireshark process running this activates\nWireshark and shows the modal dialog on top as expected, but for\nmultiple processes. Explicitly call activateWindow on the main window\nbefore calling exec() on the QMessageBox.\n\nNote that this still doesn't bring the window to the top of the desktop,\nbut instead flashes the taskbar. That's intentional Windows design:\nhttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/winuser/nf-winuser-setforegroundwindow\n\nIn Qt 5 it was possible to override the platform default\nhttps://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qwindowswindowfunctions.html#WindowActivationBehavior-enum\nbut that doesn't seem to be ported to Qt 6 yet\nhttps://www.qt.io/blog/platform-apis-in-qt-6\n\nFix #16309\n",
